        "math_academy_id": "q-110517",
        "problem": "Calculate ${f}^{\u2032}(x)$ if $f(x)=2\\sqrt{x}+5arccscx.$",
        "worked_solution": "The formula for the derivative of $arccsc$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arccscx)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2\\sqrt{x}+5arccscx) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}+5\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arccscx) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}+5(-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}-\\frac{5}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
